&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;FP&amp;amp;A Business Unit Controller&lt;/strong&gt; you will be primarily responsible for managing the business partnering relationships for the R&amp;amp;D business units including their annual budgets and quarterly forecast updates and actual performance. The ideal candidate has a strong understanding of financial processes and complex transaction flows with a desire to grow and contribute in a high-growth, fast-paced environment. This role must communicate and organize tasks well to be effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong partnership with leadership to help business owners manage their business effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead all forecasting and analysis activities for the business owners including: annual plan, quarterly forecast updates and strategic planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, analyze, and interpret financial data to evaluate operating results against budget and profitability metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide analytical insights, assess risks, and guide senior leadership in strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Corporate Finance on various projects as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide business analysis and support where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years experience in FP&amp;amp;A and business partnering, preferably in semiconductor or other manufacturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent financial modeling and business partnering skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great organization and communication skills, able to work effectively with the business to meet deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with basic GAAP concepts (revenue recognition, accruals, capitalization vs expense)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Oracle planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of financial transaction flows and financial reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong feeling of ownership over business processes and desire to improve and make them more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary range is $160,000 to $200,000 depending on experience, level, and business need. This role is eligible for discretionary bonus, incentives and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p8i6j01 paragraph&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Director, Hardware Board Validation Engineering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On-Site - San Jose, Ca&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astera Labs is seeking a Director of Hardware Board Validation Engineering to lead the development, bring-up, and validation of board products that enable rack-scale AI infrastructure. Working closely with ASIC, systems, firmware, signal integrity, power integrity, mechanical, thermal, manufacturing, and customer engineering teams, you will guide products from concept and architecture through qualification and mass production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role in a fast-moving environment. You will lead a talented engineering team while stepping in to solve complex technical problems, engage directly with customers, and improve hardware development processes. Your work will help ensure Astera Labs’ connectivity and memory products deliver reliable, high-performance systems for cloud service providers, server manufacturers, and networking OEMs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Board Product Strategy and Technical Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead board validation strategy across product definition, architecture, component selection, schematic capture, layout review, bring-up, debug, optimization, qualification, and production release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define validation plans, coverage goals, risk assessments, schedules, and exit criteria for high-speed boards, add-in cards, modules, and system platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make hands-on technical contributions to unblock critical design, validation, and customer issues in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-Speed Hardware Validation&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct board bring-up, silicon/PCB debug, system characterization, margin analysis, and performance optimization across voltage, temperature, channel, and workload conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate high-speed NRZ and PAM4 SerDes-based protocols, including PCIe Gen 3 and above and Ethernet 25G and above, as well as LPDDR4/5 or related memory interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply signal integrity, power integrity, and power architecture expertise to identify risks and drive practical solutions across circuits, power distribution, connectors, sockets, and cables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional and Customer Execution&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with ASIC, post-silicon validation, firmware, systems, mechanical, thermal, quality, compliance, manufacturing, and customer engineering teams to deliver robust board products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage key customers to understand system requirements, evaluate form factors, propose complete board solutions, and resolve issues through production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with contract manufacturers, PCB vendors, and external suppliers to ensure designs are manufacturable, testable, and scalable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Development and Productization&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, mentor, and develop a high-performing hardware engineering team while establishing clear ownership, technical standards, and execution mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive products from concept to mass production, including design reviews, validation reporting, manufacturing readiness, documentation, and post-production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve hardware development methodologies, lessons learned, and reusable validation practices across Astera Labs’ connectivity and memory product portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering or a related technical field. Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 - 15+ years of relevant experience, consistent with Astera Labs’ standardized Director level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical management experience leading hardware design, validation, or system engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system-level board design from component selection and schematic capture through board bring-up, debug, optimization, validation, and production release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in high-speed board design for enterprise, data center, server, storage, networking, or AI infrastructure systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration, technical communication, prioritization, and independent problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PCIe add-in cards, CEM cards, paddle cards, active electrical cables, servers, JBOD/JBOG systems, networking switches or routers, interconnects, or optical platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with schematic capture and PCB layout tools such as Cadence and Altium, including working knowledge of Cadence Allegro for design review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with FPGA- or MCU-based hardware design, including pin mapping, device selection, and evaluation of alternative SKUs against system requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with contract manufacturers, offshore manufacturing partners, mechanical and thermal teams, PCB vendors, quality, compliance, and supplier organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing complete high-speed channels that include ICs, sockets, connectors, cables, and customer system interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with silicon characterization and post-silicon validation teams to ensure device performance is achievable in customer systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical writing skills, including development of hardware specifications, validation reports, user guides, and other internal and customer-facing documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup experience and a proactive, hands-on, customer-focused approach to solving complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary range is $238,500 to $265,000 depending on experience, level, and business need. This role may be eligible for discretionary bonus, incentives and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p8i6j01 paragraph&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

