&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced and highly motivated Digital Design Manager to lead the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;micro-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;architecture, design, development, and delivery of IPs and Subsystems from &amp;nbsp;for next-generation switch products. This role combines deep technical expertise with strong people leadership and program management skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The successful candidate will be responsible for managing a team of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;IP &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;digital&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;design engineers while driving the successful execution of complex &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;IP &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;development programs. The role requires close collaboration with Architecture, Verification, Physical Design, DFT, Firmware, Software, Product Engineering, and SoC Integration teams to ensure delivery of high-quality IPs that meet performance, power, area, quality, and schedule objectives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;This position offers the opportunity to influence product roadmaps, establish engineering best practices, and contribute to the development of industry-leading semiconductor solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
