&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astera Labs is redefining the fabric of AI infrastructure with our Scorpio Smart Fabric Switches — purpose-built silicon that connects GPUs, CPUs, and accelerators at rack scale. As a Principal Product Applications Engineer on the Scorpio team, you will be the technical face of our switching portfolio to the world&#39;s leading hyperscalers, AI system builders, and platform partners, guiding them from first evaluation through production deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, customer-facing role at the center of one of the fastest-growing categories in semiconductors. You will lead customer system design-in and Scorpio-related debug, develop customer-facing collateral, lead cross-functional Scorpio-related initiatives, and drive and validate new features across PCIe Gen 6 / Gen 7 &amp;amp; UALink platforms — directly influencing the roadmap of a hyper-growth company powering the next generation of AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical engagements with hyperscalers, ODMs, and AI system partners from architecture discussions through design-in and evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own on-site and remote bring-up, debug, and performance tuning of Scorpio-based platforms at customer sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer requirements into actionable feedback for product, silicon, and firmware teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Silicon Validation &amp;amp; System Integration&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence post-silicon validation plans and execute system-level integration on next-generation switching platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug complex multi-domain issues spanning protocol (UALink, UCIe, PCIe Gen 6/7), signal integrity, firmware, and software stacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hardware, firmware, and SI/PI teams to root-cause issues and deliver production-ready solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Influence&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the go-to Scorpio applications expert across sales, marketing, product, and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior applications engineers and represent Astera Labs at industry forums, standards bodies, and customer executive reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author white papers, technical collateral, and training materials that scale the team&#39;s impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in product applications, systems engineering, or post-silicon validation on high-speed connectivity or networking silicon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the physical layer and high-speed serial interfaces (PCIe, Ethernet, UALink, UCIe, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with lab bring-up, debug, and system-level integration — including scopes, BERTs, and protocol analyzers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record engaging directly with hyperscaler, cloud, or Tier-1 OEM/ODM customers on complex technical deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to translate deep technical detail into clear customer-facing narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS or PhD in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with PCIe Gen 6 / Gen 7, UALink, or UCIe protocols and compliance testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI/ML rack-scale architectures, GPU fabrics, and accelerator interconnects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting and automation experience (Python, shell) for validation and diagnostics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background contributing to standards bodies (PCI-SIG, UALink Consortium, UCIe) or authoring technical publications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p8i6j01 paragraph&quot;&gt;Salary range is $165,000 to $210,000 CAN depending on experience, level, and business need. This role may be eligible for discretionary bonuses, incentives, and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astera Labs is seeking a Principal Engineering, Hardware NPI Program Manager to lead complex hardware programs from design release through productization, validation, customer readiness, and launch. This highly visible role combines technical NPI expertise with cross-functional program leadership to deliver purpose-built connectivity solutions for rack-scale AI infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bring structure to programs spanning product, hardware, systems, manufacturing, operations, supply chain, quality, finance, and customer-facing teams. You will own integrated plans, dependencies, risks, decisions, and outcomes while driving accountability across a fast-moving, globally distributed organization. Your work will turn engineering intent into predictable, customer-ready hardware and help Astera scale new connectivity platforms with speed, quality, and confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPI Program Planning and Execution&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define PCBA program schedules, build quantities, milestones, budgets, dependencies, and readiness criteria from concept through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead prototype and new-product builds through PCB and PCBA fabrication, assembly, bring-up, validation, shipment readiness, and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish readiness reviews, decision forums, dashboards, and escalation paths that keep teams aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop recovery recommendations when material shortages, engineering changes, supplier constraints, or other risks threaten delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Product Execution&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align product, hardware, systems, validation, manufacturing, quality, supply chain, finance, operations, and customer-facing teams around shared outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify blockers early, assign accountable owners, drive decisions to closure, and escalate issues with clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate concise, decision-oriented updates to technical teams, senior leaders, executives, customers, contract manufacturers, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manufacturing Readiness and Supplier Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm that bill of materials, part numbers, fabrication and assembly data, suppliers, work instructions, deviations, engineering changes, and approvals are complete before each build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highlight and resolve manufacturing issues involving component sourcing, design for manufacturability, programming, assembly, rework, traceability, and hardware logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary program and technical contact for contract manufacturers, rework providers, and other external partners while maintaining accountability for commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence and Team Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve program-management processes, documentation, repositories, reporting, and performance metrics so execution becomes more predictable, measurable, and searchable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify repetitive or error-prone work that can be standardized or automated, and partner with data, software, and applied-AI teams to improve dashboards, milestone tracking, document workflows, and program knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach team members on readiness, documentation, supplier communication, decision-making, and escalation practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, computer science, operations, or a related field; equivalent practical experience may be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–12 years of experience in hardware NPI, technical program management, manufacturing engineering, product operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience guiding hardware products or builds through development, validation, manufacturing, or launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of hardware development, PCB/PCBA manufacturing, bills of materials, engineering changes, supplier coordination, and manufacturing release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage integrated schedules, milestones, risks, action items, budgets, and cross-functional dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence teams without direct authority and operate effectively in a fast-paced environment with changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel internationally as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-speed networking, PCIe Gen 6 or Gen 7, UALink, optical or cable connectivity, retimers, ASICs, compute platforms, data centers, or AI infrastructure hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of physical-layer considerations for high-speed interconnects, including signal integrity, board-level debug, prototype rework, BGA processing, X-ray review, or failure analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with customer programs, product launches, strategic initiatives, cost and operational improvement programs, product lifecycle activities, quality, RMA, or EOL execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint, Project, SharePoint, Power BI, and Teams for planning, reporting, documentation, collaboration, and executive communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building dashboards, data pipelines, workflow automation, or AI-assisted engineering tools, as well as managing prototype budgets, purchase requests, purchase orders, supplier quotes, or forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers, interns, or cross-functional teams and strengthening execution practices across a growing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

