&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Astera Labs is redefining the connectivity that powers rack-scale AI infrastructure, and analog design is at the heart of it. As a Principal Analog Design Engineer, you will architect and design the high-performance analog and mixed-signal circuits that anchor our SerDes, PHY, and high-speed I/O — the silicon building blocks that move data at the speed AI demands. Your work directly shapes the performance, power, and reliability of products deployed in the world&#39;s most advanced data centers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;This is a high-impact, hands-on role at a hyper-growth company purpose-built for AI connectivity. You will own designs from concept through silicon bring-up, set the technical bar for the analog team, and mentor engineers as we scale. If you want your circuits to enable the next generation of AI compute, this is where that happens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wnfdntf&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analog &amp;amp; Mixed-Signal Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wnfdntf&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Architect and design high-speed analog and mixed-signal circuits including PLLs, LDOs, references, high-speed SerDes building blocks, ADCs/DACs, and clocking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Drive circuit design from specification and architecture through schematic, layout supervision, and verification across PVT corners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Develop robust designs in advanced FinFET process nodes with attention to power, area, and performance trade-offs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Silicon Execution &amp;amp; Validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wnfdntf&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Lead silicon bring-up, characterization, and debug, partnering with validation and product engineering to root-cause and resolve issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Define and execute test plans to correlate silicon performance against design targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wnfdntf&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Set analog design methodology, review standards, and best practices across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Partner cross-functionally with digital, physical design, systems, and architecture teams to deliver full-chip solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Mentor and guide junior engineers, elevating the technical capability of the analog organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wnfdntf&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;MS or PhD in Electrical Engineering or a related field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;8+ years of experience in analog and mixed-signal integrated circuit design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Proven track record designing high-speed analog circuits such as PLLs, SerDes front-ends, data converters, references, or regulators in advanced CMOS/FinFET nodes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of physical-layer design principles, signal integrity, and high-speed I/O.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Proficiency with industry-standard design and simulation tools (e.g., Cadence Virtuoso, Spectre) and solid layout/parasitic-aware design skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wnfdntf&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Experience taking multiple analog/mixed-signal designs through full production tape-out and high-volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Expertise in high-speed serial link design (PCIe, Ethernet, UALink, UCIe) and associated PHY architectures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Familiarity with silicon debug, ATE test development, and design-for-test techniques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Experience mentoring engineers and leading technical design reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Excellent communication skills and a collaborative, ownership-driven mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Salary range is $170,000 to $210,000 depending on experience, level, and business need. This role may be eligible for discretionary bonus, incentives and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astera Labs is seeking a principal board NPI planner to drive material and production readiness for new hardware products, from early engineering builds through manufacturing ramp. You will turn complex requirements into executable plans, ensuring PCBA components, assemblies, suppliers, and build schedules are aligned to program milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is central to bringing purpose-built connectivity solutions to market quickly and reliably as Astera Labs scales its rack-scale AI infrastructure portfolio. You will work across engineering, operations, procurement, and quality to support order fulfillment, surface risks early, resolve constraints, and improve launch execution in a fast-moving semiconductor environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Planning &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Own PCBA planning activities through production ramp readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Build and maintain detailed build plans covering BOM readiness, material availability, purchase orders, supplier commitments, and production milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Track planning-system transactions, inventory, shortages, and material status to keep the builds on schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Support order fulfillment against internal and external demand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Support local manufacturing activities and resolve execution issues as they arise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Manufacturing Coordination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Partner with hardware engineering, operations, procurement, and the internal contract manufacturing team to align demand, supply, and execution plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Coordinate PCBA readiness across component suppliers, PCB and assembly partners, and test or manufacturing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Support build execution by monitoring work-in-progress, finished goods, configuration changes, and handoffs into sustaining or high-volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Risk Management &amp;amp; Launch Communication&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Identify material shortages, supplier constraints, capacity gaps, and schedule risks, then drive mitigation plans to protect launch milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Prepare clear status reports, readiness assessments, and escalation materials for program and operations reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Analyze supply, delivery, and cost tradeoffs and recommend actions that improve schedule predictability and inventory efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain, Engineering, Operations, Business, or a related field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· 8+ years of experience in NPI planning, supply chain planning, production planning, or manufacturing operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience in PCBA hardware manufacturing, specifically within electronics assembly and contract manufacturing environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Strong working knowledge of material requirements planning, supply-demand planning, inventory management, and supplier coordination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience building and managing detailed schedules across multiple cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Advanced Microsoft Excel skills and hands-on experience with ERP or MRP systems, with strong analytical and communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience supporting new product introductions for data center or AI infrastructure products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Familiarity with PCBAs, bills of material, approved vendor lists, engineering changes, component lifecycle management, and manufacturing readiness gates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience working with global suppliers, contract manufacturers, and manufacturing partners in Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience creating planning dashboards, shortage reports, and data-driven operating metrics using Microsoft tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Ability to influence cross-functional teams, manage competing priorities, and drive timely resolution in a high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astera Labs is seeking a principal board NPI planner to drive material and production readiness for new hardware products, from early engineering builds through manufacturing ramp. You will turn complex requirements into executable plans, ensuring PCBA components, assemblies, suppliers, and build schedules are aligned to program milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is central to bringing purpose-built connectivity solutions to market quickly and reliably as Astera Labs scales its rack-scale AI infrastructure portfolio. You will work across engineering, operations, procurement, and quality to support order fulfillment, surface risks early, resolve constraints, and improve launch execution in a fast-moving semiconductor environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Planning &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Own PCBA planning activities through production ramp readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Build and maintain detailed build plans covering BOM readiness, material availability, purchase orders, supplier commitments, and production milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Track planning-system transactions, inventory, shortages, and material status to keep the builds on schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Support order fulfillment against internal and external demand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Support local manufacturing activities and resolve execution issues as they arise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Manufacturing Coordination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Partner with hardware engineering, operations, procurement, and the internal contract manufacturing team to align demand, supply, and execution plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Coordinate PCBA readiness across component suppliers, PCB and assembly partners, and test or manufacturing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Support build execution by monitoring work-in-progress, finished goods, configuration changes, and handoffs into sustaining or high-volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Risk Management &amp;amp; Launch Communication&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Identify material shortages, supplier constraints, capacity gaps, and schedule risks, then drive mitigation plans to protect launch milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Prepare clear status reports, readiness assessments, and escalation materials for program and operations reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o Analyze supply, delivery, and cost tradeoffs and recommend actions that improve schedule predictability and inventory efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Bachelor’s degree in Supply Chain, Engineering, Operations, Business, or a related field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· 8+ years of experience in NPI planning, supply chain planning, production planning, or manufacturing operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience in PCBA hardware manufacturing, specifically within electronics assembly and contract manufacturing environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Strong working knowledge of material requirements planning, supply-demand planning, inventory management, and supplier coordination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience building and managing detailed schedules across multiple cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Advanced Microsoft Excel skills and hands-on experience with ERP or MRP systems, with strong analytical and communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience supporting new product introductions for data center or AI infrastructure products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Familiarity with PCBAs, bills of material, approved vendor lists, engineering changes, component lifecycle management, and manufacturing readiness gates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience working with global suppliers, contract manufacturers, and manufacturing partners in Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience creating planning dashboards, shortage reports, and data-driven operating metrics using Microsoft tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Ability to influence cross-functional teams, manage competing priorities, and drive timely resolution in a high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

