&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and hands-on &lt;strong&gt;Principal Product Engineer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to lead and develop next generation high-speed, high performance and low power semiconductor products in advanced process node. The ideal candidate possesses breadth of industry experience in high-speed product development in the field of product and/or test engineering, can apply fundamentals in circuit, ATE, and test program to aid problem solving, and is a self-driven, result focused go-getter in the pursuit of goals and objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 8 years of experience in the field of post silicon product development dealing with high-speed I/O (product test or validation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have gone through at least one cycle of full product development life cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong academic/technical background in electrical or computer engineering; Bachelor’s is required; MS preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills that involve system level analysis with test hardware, test program and DUT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital and analog circuit level understanding for DUT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent team player with great communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional attitude with the ability to prioritize a dynamic list of multiple tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Experience&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with using the Advantest 93k ATE platform with specific skills updating ATE test programs for wafer sort and final test solutions or similar ATE platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detailed mindset monitoring device ATE test yields, ATE test time, device quality and rolling out new ATE test programs using consistent BKMs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data analysis skills using tools such as JMP or Spotfire calculating limits and drawing conclusions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Energetic work mindset meeting the demands of shipping quality parts to Astera Labs’ customers through the manufacturing stage of development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience in product/package qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on knowledge of NRZ/PAM4 SerDes protocols like PCIe (Gen3 and above), Ethernet (25G and above), etc. and/or memory interfaces such as (LP)DDR5/4&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with silicon validation teams to ensure device performance meets production requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Firmware development in C/C++, scripting in Python, or other equivalent programming experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The base salary range is USD 185,00 - USD 240,000. Your base salary will be determined based on your location, experience, and the pay of employees in similar positions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Principal Product Manager, Fiber Connectivity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;San Jose, California, United States&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job Summary:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Astera Labs is redefining the connectivity fabric of rack-scale AI infrastructure, with optical connectivity becoming increasingly important to the next generation of scale-up and scale out systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Product Manager for Fiber Connectivity, you will own the link between AI system architecture and commercial product adoption. You will define a portfolio of passive optical connectivity solutions, set customer-driven product requirements, and drive products from concept through qualification, deployment, and production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Optical connectivity is becoming a system-level architecture decision in AI infrastructure, not simply a component choice. This role spans optical performance, system integration, manufacturing scale, supply chain, customer qualification, and commercial execution. You will work with hyperscalers, AI infrastructure companies and optical ecosystem partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Define the product strategy and multi-year roadmap for passive optical connectivity at the fiber-to-chip and system interfaces of high-density AI infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Identify target applications, market opportunities, technology transitions, and competitive threats, serving as the voice of the customer for hyperscalers, AI infrastructure companies, system OEMs and ecosystem partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Set customer-driven product attribute targets and make clear tradeoffs across optical performance, density, cost, manufacturability, reliability, supply chain, adoption, and time to market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Develop go-to-market strategy and launch plans, including market assessment, competitive analysis, positioning, technical content, and sales enablement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Execute product development from concept through requirements, development, qualification, customer deployment, production ramp, and sustaining support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Lead cross-functional relationships across optical, mechanical, electrical, systems, manufacturing, operations, quality, supply chain, applications, sales, and finance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Establish manufacturing, supplier, automation, quality, reliability, test, yield, capacity, and cost-reduction strategies for high-volume production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with sales and applications teams to secure design wins, support customer commitments, and drive adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, physics, materials science, business, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in product management, product line management, engineering, applications, business development, or a related function.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience developing and commercializing complex hardware products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience in optics, photonics, fiber optics, optical connectivity, optical packaging, or a related technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience working across engineering, manufacturing, operations, supply chain, sales, and commercial organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and cross-functional leadership skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Willingness to travel internationally as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or advanced technical degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market knowledge of AI, cloud, networking, data center, server, and high performance computing infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Strong understanding of passive optical connectivity, optical coupling, fiber assemblies, connectors, alignment, and optical and mechanical tolerances.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience with co-packaged optics, near-package optics, optical I/O, scale-up optical interconnects, or related emerging architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-volume manufacturing, supplier qualification, new product introduction, or production ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work directly with hyperscalers, major system companies and optical ecosystem partners&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary range is $185,000 to $240,000 depending on experience, level, and business need. This role may be eligible for discretionary bonus, incentives and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

