&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Astera Labs is seeking a dynamic and technical Manager, System Validation Engineering to lead our post-silicon and system validation teams in Haifa.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;In this leadership role, you will direct engineering teams responsible for validating high-performance PCIe and connectivity fabric switch products built for rack-scale AI and cloud data centers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;You will combine hands-on technical oversight with strong people management, guiding engineers through validation strategy, automated test execution, deep root-cause investigations, and direct customer integration support. This is a critical leadership position to shape our validation methodologies, scale automation infrastructure, and ensure the flawless execution and launch of purpose-built connectivity silicon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Success Looks Like&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Execution &amp;amp; On-Time Delivery: New silicon, platforms, and AI fabric switch solutions are brought up and certified on schedule with rigorous, reproducible validation results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Scale: Engineering talent is mentored, engaged, and effectively deployed across multiple projects, fostering a culture of technical excellence, accountability, and innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Efficiency: Test suites and infrastructure are scaled to maximize test coverage, minimize manual effort, and drive down test cycle times.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Customer Trust &amp;amp; Resolution: Complex cross-functional system issues are resolved rapidly through data-backed root-cause analysis, resulting in high customer satisfaction during integration and deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Team Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Lead, mentor, and grow a team of high-performing System Validation Engineers at Haifa&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Drive resource planning, project scheduling, engineer capacity tracking, and milestone execution across multiple complex silicon programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Foster strong cross-functional alignment with Silicon Design, Firmware, Software, Hardware, Product, and Applications teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Attract, hire, and develop top engineering talent while championing technical growth and career development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Validation Strategy &amp;amp; Planning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Oversee the creation of comprehensive validation plans for AI fabric switch products covering functionality, performance, reliability, stress, and interoperability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Translate complex customer and system requirements into measurable test objectives, coverage goals, and product certification criteria.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Establish clear, data-driven reporting metrics, status dashboards, and specification-compliance assessments for executive leadership and key customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guide technical execution for silicon and platform bring-up activities, verifying boot and runtime behavior on x86 and ARM systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Oversee complex debugging across PCIe, NVMe, Ethernet, firmware, hardware, and system layers using advanced lab equipment and CPU-based tool suites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Drive systematic root-cause problem solving, guiding engineers through structured experiment design to isolate and resolve complex silicon, firmware, and board-level issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Scale validation infrastructure supporting test orchestration, advanced data collection, statistical analysis, and automated report generation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Continually optimize validation workflows and lab debug tools to accelerate issue resolution and improve regression coverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;24&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;8+ years of total experience in silicon product development, post-silicon validation, or system engineering for server, storage, networking, or AI infrastructure applications, including 4+ years of technical leadership or people management experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience leading engineering teams, managing project schedules, and driving execution in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Proven track record with complex silicon and system bring-up, validation, and laboratory debug methodologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Strong Python automation background for test orchestration, bench control, and data analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Exceptional communication, stakeholder management, and cross-functional leadership skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Astera Labs (NASDAQ: ALAB) provides rack-scale AI infrastructure through purpose-built connectivity solutions. By collaborating with hyperscalers and ecosystem partners, Astera Labs enables organizations to unlock the full potential of modern AI. Astera Labs’ Intelligent Connectivity Platform integrates CXL®, Ethernet, NVLink, PCIe®, and UALink™ semiconductor-based technologies with the company’s COSMOS software suite to unify diverse components into cohesive, flexible systems that deliver end-to-end scale-up, and scale-out connectivity. The company’s custom connectivity solutions business complements its standards-based portfolio, enabling customers to deploy tailored architectures to meet their unique infrastructure requirements. Discover more at &lt;a id=&quot;menurhut&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;http://www.asteralabs.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.asteralabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Physical Design Engineer to join our high-performance design team working on next-generation transceiver IPs targeting the TSMC 3nm and advanced technology nodes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perform block-level and top-level physical implementation including floorplanning, placement, clock tree synthesis (CTS), routing, and physical verification for high-speed designs in advanced technology nodes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with RTL and STA teams to ensure clean handoffs and support timing, area, and power convergence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply advanced physical design techniques to support multiple voltage and frequency domains, hierarchical design, and physical-aware synthesis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work on key physical design areas including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EM/IR analysis and power grid optimization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Congestion analysis and mitigation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clock skew optimization and clock quality improvement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;RC extraction-aware placement and routing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Integrate IPs and top-level blocks with attention to physical interfaces, constraints, and timing alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support floorplan development and chip partitioning for high-speed transceiver designs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perform ECO implementation and assist with tapeout signoff activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure DRC, LVS, ANT, CELL, and ERC clean databases using industry-standard physical verification tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use industry-standard tools such as ICC2, Innovus, Voltus, RedHawk, and Calibre for implementation and signoff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and maintain automation scripts in Tcl, Python, or Perl to improve physical design flows and productivity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of experience in physical design, preferably with advanced technology nodes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong experience with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Floorplanning, placement, CTS, routing, and IR drop mitigation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Signoff checks such as DRC, LVS, ANT, and ERC, along with debugging&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Timing closure support in collaboration with STA teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on use of tools such as Synopsys ICC2, Cadence Innovus, Calibre, and Voltus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience integrating high-speed IPs such as SerDes or PHYs into SoC or chiplet-based environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working on high-frequency datapath and DSP-related designs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid scripting skills for automation and productivity enhancement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Good problem-solving skills and the ability to work effectively in cross-functional teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We know that creativity and innovation happen more often when teams include diverse ideas, backgrounds, and experiences, and we actively encourage everyone with relevant experience to apply, including people of color, LGBTQ+ and non-binary people, veterans, parents, and individuals with disabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

